{"packet_id": "D052-01", "doc_id": "D052", "jurisdiction": "MA", "category": "application_screening_fees", "lifecycle": "enacted", "title": "Cap on amounts required at or before the start of a tenancy", "requirement": "At or before a tenancy begins, a landlord or the landlord's agent may require only first month's rent, last month's rent at the same rate, a security deposit equal to first month's rent, and the cost of a key and lock.", "key_value": "1st month rent + last month rent at same rate + deposit equal to 1 month's rent + key/lock cost", "coverage_conditions": "Residential real property in Massachusetts; limits what a lessor or the lessor's agent may require from a tenant or prospective tenant at or before the tenancy begins.", "applicability": {"built_on_or_before": null, "built_after": null, "date_basis": null, "min_units": null, "max_units": null, "owner_dependent": false, "other": null}, "exemptions": null, "penalty": "Forfeiture of the right to retain the deposit, and treble damages plus 5% interest, court costs and reasonable attorney's fees, for a lessor who uses or enforces a lease provision conflicting with this section or seeks a waiver of it.", "effective_date": null, "citation": "G.L. c. 186, § 15B: upfront payments required at or before tenancy", "quoted_span": "(b) At or prior to the commencement of any tenancy, no lessor or agent of the lessor may require a tenant or prospective tenant to pay, to the lessor or to an agent of the lessor, any amount in excess of the following: \n(i) rent for the first full month of occupancy;  and, \n(ii) rent for the last full month of occupancy calculated at the same rate as the first month;  and,", "interaction": null, "confidence": 0.95, "conflict_flag": false, "conflict_note": null}
{"packet_id": "D052-01", "doc_id": "D052", "jurisdiction": "MA", "category": "security_deposits", "lifecycle": "enacted", "title": "Security deposit cap equal to one month's rent", "requirement": "A landlord may not require, and no successor may later demand, a security deposit greater than one month's rent; the deposit must be deposited under subsection (3) and the tenant given the statement of condition under subsection (2).", "key_value": "1 month's rent", "coverage_conditions": "Residential real property in Massachusetts; security deposits received from a tenant or prospective tenant.", "applicability": {"built_on_or_before": null, "built_after": null, "date_basis": null, "min_units": null, "max_units": null, "owner_dependent": false, "other": null}, "exemptions": null, "penalty": "Forfeiture of the right to retain the deposit, and treble damages plus 5% interest, court costs and reasonable attorney's fees, for a lessor who uses or enforces a lease provision conflicting with this section or seeks a waiver of it.", "effective_date": null, "citation": "G.L. c. 186, § 15B: security deposit maximum", "quoted_span": "a security deposit equal to the first month's rent provided that such security deposit is deposited as required by subsection (3) and that the tenant is given the statement of condition as required by subsection (2)", "interaction": null, "confidence": 0.95, "conflict_flag": false, "conflict_note": null}
{"packet_id": "D052-01", "doc_id": "D052", "jurisdiction": "MA", "category": "security_deposits", "lifecycle": "enacted", "title": "Fee in lieu of a security deposit capped at one month's rent", "requirement": "Regulations may let a landlord and tenant agree to a fee instead of a security deposit, but the fee and any recurring payments may not total more than one month's rent, must be optional for both, and the tenant may still choose a full deposit.", "key_value": "1 month's rent total cap", "coverage_conditions": "Residential tenancies where the executive office of housing and livable communities authorizes a fee in lieu of a security deposit by regulation; it must be offered to every applicant whose application is approved.", "applicability": {"built_on_or_before": null, "built_after": null, "date_basis": null, "min_units": null, "max_units": null, "owner_dependent": false, "other": null}, "exemptions": null, "penalty": null, "effective_date": "2025-08-01", "citation": "G.L. c. 186, § 15B: fee in lieu of security deposit", "quoted_span": "limit the total sum of the fee or recurring payments, regardless of the duration of the lease and any extensions thereto, to an amount not to exceed 1 month's rent", "interaction": null, "confidence": 0.85, "conflict_flag": false, "conflict_note": null}
{"packet_id": "D052-01", "doc_id": "D052", "jurisdiction": "MA", "category": "security_deposits", "lifecycle": "enacted", "title": "Security deposit held in a separate interest-bearing account with 5% interest", "requirement": "A landlord must hold a security deposit in a separate interest-bearing Massachusetts bank account beyond creditors' claims, give a receipt within thirty days, and pay the tenant five per cent yearly interest or the lesser amount the bank paid.", "key_value": "5% per year", "coverage_conditions": "Residential real property in Massachusetts; deposits held for one year or longer from the commencement of the term of the tenancy.", "applicability": {"built_on_or_before": null, "built_after": null, "date_basis": null, "min_units": null, "max_units": null, "owner_dependent": false, "other": null}, "exemptions": null, "penalty": "Failure to comply with subsection (3) entitles the tenant to the immediate return of the security deposit.", "effective_date": null, "citation": "G.L. c. 186, § 15B: security deposit account and interest", "quoted_span": "A lessor of residential real property who holds a security deposit pursuant to this section for a period of one year or longer from the commencement of the term of the tenancy shall, beginning with the first day of the tenancy, pay interest at the rate of five per cent per year, or other such lesser amount of interest as has been received from the bank where the deposit has been held payable to the tenant at the end of each year of the tenancy.", "interaction": null, "confidence": 0.95, "conflict_flag": false, "conflict_note": null}
{"packet_id": "D052-01", "doc_id": "D052", "jurisdiction": "MA", "category": "security_deposits", "lifecycle": "enacted", "title": "Return of security deposit within thirty days of termination", "requirement": "Within thirty days after the tenancy ends the landlord must return the deposit or balance, may deduct only unpaid rent or water charges, tax-escalation increases and tenant damage, and must give a sworn itemized damage list for any deduction.", "key_value": "30 days", "coverage_conditions": "Tenancies at will and tenancies ending as specified in a valid written lease of residential real property in Massachusetts.", "applicability": {"built_on_or_before": null, "built_after": null, "date_basis": null, "min_units": null, "max_units": null, "owner_dependent": false, "other": null}, "exemptions": null, "penalty": "A lessor who fails to return the deposit within thirty days forfeits the right to retain any portion of it and owes three times the deposit or balance, plus 5% interest, court costs and reasonable attorney's fees.", "effective_date": null, "citation": "G.L. c. 186, § 15B: return of security deposit and permitted deductions", "quoted_span": "The lessor shall, within thirty days after the termination of occupancy under a tenancy-at-will or the end of the tenancy as specified in a valid written lease agreement, return to the tenant the security deposit or any balance thereof", "interaction": null, "confidence": 0.95, "conflict_flag": false, "conflict_note": null}
{"packet_id": "D052-01", "doc_id": "D052", "jurisdiction": "MA", "category": "security_deposits", "lifecycle": "enacted", "title": "Transfer of security deposit to a successor landlord with 45-day notice", "requirement": "A landlord who transfers the property must pass the security deposit and accrued interest to the successor, who must notify the tenant in writing within forty-five days and is liable for holding and returning the deposit.", "key_value": "45 days' notice to tenant", "coverage_conditions": "Dwelling units where a lessor holding a security deposit transfers the interest by sale, assignment, death, appointment of a receiver or trustee in bankruptcy, or otherwise.", "applicability": {"built_on_or_before": null, "built_after": null, "date_basis": null, "min_units": null, "max_units": null, "owner_dependent": false, "other": null}, "exemptions": "Does not apply to a city or town acquiring title under chapter sixty, or to a foreclosing mortgagee or mortgagee in possession that is a financial institution chartered by the commonwealth or the United States.", "penalty": "A successor who does not receive the transfer assumes liability for paying the deposit to the tenant; failure to transfer or comply with subsection (5) brings three times the deposit, plus 5% interest, court costs and reasonable attorney's fees.", "effective_date": null, "citation": "G.L. c. 186, § 15B: transfer of security deposit to successor in interest", "quoted_span": "The successor in interest shall, within forty-five days from the date of said transfer, notify the tenant who made such security deposit that such security deposit was transferred to him and that he is holding said security deposit.", "interaction": null, "confidence": 0.95, "conflict_flag": false, "conflict_note": null}
